{"module":"reparations","voice":"female","duration":205.1,"segments":[{"el":"title","text":"Repair and reparations","start":0.0,"end":1.74,"words":[[0.05,0.45],[0.45,0.69],[0.69,1.58]]},{"el":"intro","text":"Reparations is one of the most debated ideas in American politics.","start":2.54,"end":7.03,"words":[[2.59,3.33],[3.33,3.47],[3.47,3.67],[3.67,3.81],[3.81,3.94],[3.94,4.28],[4.28,4.82],[4.82,5.22],[5.22,5.36],[5.36,5.9],[5.9,6.5]]},{"el":"intro","text":"This lesson lays out what the term means, what has actually been done, and the main arguments on each side, so you can decide for yourself.","start":7.38,"end":15.24,"words":[[7.43,7.64],[7.64,7.97],[7.97,8.24],[8.24,8.44],[8.44,8.64],[8.64,8.77],[8.77,8.97],[8.97,9.31],[9.54,9.74],[9.74,9.94],[9.94,10.48],[10.48,10.68],[10.68,10.94],[11.18,11.38],[11.38,11.51],[11.51,11.78],[11.78,12.38],[12.38,12.52],[12.52,12.72],[12.72,13.05],[13.28,13.49],[13.49,13.62],[13.62,13.82],[13.82,14.22],[14.22,14.35],[14.35,14.82]]},{"el":"h0","text":"What “repair” can mean","start":15.59,"end":17.03,"words":[[15.64,15.93],[15.93,16.4],[16.4,16.68],[16.68,16.96]]},{"el":"s0","text":"The United Nations' 2005 principles on remedies for serious human rights violations list five forms of reparation: restitution (restoring what was lost), compensation, rehabilitation (such as health care), satisfaction (including apologies, truth-telling and memorials), and guarantees that it won't happen again.","start":17.73,"end":39.65,"words":[[17.78,17.94],[17.94,18.54],[18.54,19.08],[19.08,20.07],[20.07,20.83],[20.83,20.98],[20.98,21.51],[21.51,21.66],[21.66,22.27],[22.27,22.73],[22.73,23.11],[23.11,23.95],[23.95,24.25],[24.25,24.56],[24.56,24.86],[24.86,25.01],[25.01,25.85],[26.12,26.95],[26.95,27.56],[27.56,27.79],[27.79,28.02],[28.02,28.4],[28.66,29.65],[29.92,30.98],[30.98,31.29],[31.29,31.44],[31.44,31.75],[31.75,32.05],[32.32,33.15],[33.15,33.76],[33.76,34.52],[34.79,35.47],[35.47,35.7],[35.7,36.54],[36.81,37.03],[37.03,37.64],[37.64,37.87],[37.87,38.02],[38.02,38.4],[38.4,38.78],[38.78,39.16]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Cash payments are only one of them.","start":40.0,"end":42.11,"words":[[40.0,40.2],[40.2,40.72],[40.72,40.78],[40.78,41.1],[41.1,41.3],[41.3,41.43],[41.43,41.69]]},{"el":"h1","text":"Precedents","start":43.01,"end":44.04,"words":[[43.06,43.9]]},{"el":"s1","text":"West Germany's 1952 agreement to pay Israel and Holocaust survivors.","start":44.74,"end":50.08,"words":[[44.79,45.08],[45.08,45.66],[45.66,46.68],[46.68,47.26],[47.26,47.41],[47.41,47.63],[47.63,48.07],[48.07,48.28],[48.28,48.87],[48.87,49.52]]},{"el":"s1","text":"The Civil Liberties Act of 1988: an apology and $20,000 for each surviving Japanese American incarcerated during World War II.","start":50.43,"end":60.62,"words":[[50.47,50.62],[50.62,50.98],[50.98,51.5],[51.5,51.72],[51.72,51.87],[51.87,53.04],[53.3,53.45],[53.45,54.04],[54.04,54.26],[54.26,55.51],[55.51,55.65],[55.65,55.87],[55.87,56.46],[56.46,57.05],[57.05,57.64],[57.64,58.52],[58.52,59.04],[59.04,59.33],[59.33,59.48],[59.48,60.14]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Florida's 1994 compensation for Rosewood survivors.","start":60.97,"end":65.25,"words":[[60.99,61.56],[61.56,62.63],[62.63,63.49],[63.49,63.63],[63.63,64.13],[64.13,64.77]]},{"el":"s1","text":"North Carolina (2013) and Virginia (2015) compensating survivors of forced sterilization.","start":65.6,"end":72.72,"words":[[65.65,65.86],[65.86,66.49],[66.49,67.25],[67.5,67.7],[67.7,68.26],[68.26,69.09],[69.34,70.17],[70.17,70.72],[70.72,70.86],[70.86,71.14],[71.14,72.18]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Chicago's 2015 reparations for people tortured by police commander Jon Burge's officers, including payments, counseling and a public memorial.","start":73.07,"end":83.19,"words":[[73.07,73.67],[73.67,74.56],[74.56,75.37],[75.37,75.52],[75.52,75.89],[75.89,76.34],[76.34,76.56],[76.56,76.93],[76.93,77.45],[77.45,77.74],[77.74,78.19],[78.19,78.71],[78.97,79.56],[79.56,80.23],[80.49,81.15],[81.15,81.38],[81.38,81.52],[81.52,81.97],[81.97,82.71]]},{"el":"h2","text":"Recent efforts","start":84.09,"end":85.46,"words":[[84.14,84.78],[84.78,85.32]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Evanston, Illinois, began a housing reparations program in 2021, funded by a cannabis tax.","start":86.16,"end":93.42,"words":[[86.22,86.82],[87.06,87.53],[87.77,88.1],[88.1,88.24],[88.24,88.64],[88.64,89.38],[89.38,89.92],[89.92,90.06],[90.06,91.14],[91.37,91.78],[91.78,91.98],[91.98,92.11],[92.11,92.59],[92.59,92.92]]},{"el":"s2","text":"California's Reparations Task Force issued a final report in 2023 with more than 100 recommendations; the legislature has acted on a few.","start":93.77,"end":103.62,"words":[[93.77,94.51],[94.51,95.31],[95.31,95.61],[95.61,95.83],[95.83,96.12],[96.12,96.27],[96.27,96.71],[96.71,97.07],[97.07,97.22],[97.22,98.32],[98.32,98.54],[98.54,98.69],[98.69,98.91],[98.91,99.64],[99.64,100.74],[101.0,101.14],[101.14,101.95],[101.95,102.17],[102.17,102.54],[102.54,102.68],[102.68,102.83],[102.83,103.12]]},{"el":"s2","text":"In 2025, Tulsa's first Black mayor proposed a privately funded Greenwood Trust to invest in the district destroyed in 1921.","start":103.97,"end":113.84,"words":[[104.02,104.17],[104.17,105.46],[105.72,106.18],[106.18,106.48],[106.48,106.78],[106.78,107.01],[107.01,107.61],[107.61,107.77],[107.77,108.45],[108.45,108.9],[108.9,109.43],[109.43,109.81],[109.81,109.96],[109.96,110.42],[110.42,110.57],[110.57,110.72],[110.72,111.32],[111.32,111.93],[111.93,112.08],[112.08,113.37]]},{"el":"s2","text":"H.R.","start":114.19,"end":115.12,"words":[[114.24,114.62]]},{"el":"s2","text":"40, a bill to create a federal commission to study reparations, was first introduced by Representative John Conyers in 1989 and has been reintroduced in every Congress since.","start":115.47,"end":128.2,"words":[[115.47,115.84],[116.11,116.26],[116.26,116.48],[116.48,116.63],[116.63,117.16],[117.16,117.31],[117.31,117.83],[117.83,118.36],[118.36,118.51],[118.51,118.89],[118.89,119.79],[120.05,120.28],[120.28,120.58],[120.58,121.33],[121.33,121.55],[121.55,122.53],[122.53,122.83],[122.83,123.36],[123.36,123.51],[123.51,124.64],[124.64,124.86],[124.86,125.09],[125.09,125.31],[125.31,126.29],[126.29,126.44],[126.44,126.74],[126.74,127.27],[127.27,127.64]]},{"el":"h3","text":"The arguments","start":129.1,"end":130.32,"words":[[129.2,129.38],[129.38,130.2]]},{"el":"s3","text":"For: the harms were done by governments through documented policies (slavery's protection in law, Jim Crow, redlining, exclusion from the GI Bill), their effects on wealth are measurable today, and the U.S. has paid reparations to other groups it harmed.","start":131.02,"end":147.17,"words":[[131.06,131.28],[131.53,131.67],[131.67,131.96],[131.96,132.11],[132.11,132.32],[132.32,132.54],[132.54,133.26],[133.26,133.48],[133.48,134.27],[134.27,134.78],[134.78,135.43],[135.43,136.07],[136.07,136.22],[136.22,136.44],[136.69,136.98],[136.98,137.34],[137.59,138.31],[138.56,139.21],[139.21,139.5],[139.5,139.65],[139.65,140.08],[140.08,140.37],[140.62,140.84],[140.84,141.27],[141.27,141.41],[141.41,141.7],[141.7,141.77],[141.77,142.42],[142.42,142.86],[143.11,143.32],[143.32,143.47],[143.47,143.83],[144.19,144.41],[144.41,144.69],[144.69,145.49],[145.49,145.63],[145.63,145.85],[145.85,146.21],[146.21,146.35],[146.35,146.71]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Against or skeptical: difficulty deciding who is eligible and who pays, the cost, the argument that today's taxpayers didn't commit the wrongs, and a preference for programs based on income or place rather than race.","start":147.52,"end":161.41,"words":[[147.57,148.02],[148.02,148.1],[148.1,148.85],[149.11,149.79],[149.79,150.39],[150.39,150.54],[150.54,150.69],[150.69,151.37],[151.37,151.59],[151.59,151.74],[151.74,152.12],[152.38,152.53],[152.53,152.91],[153.17,153.32],[153.32,153.92],[153.92,154.15],[154.15,154.6],[154.6,155.27],[155.27,155.65],[155.65,156.03],[156.03,156.18],[156.18,156.55],[156.82,157.04],[157.04,157.19],[157.19,157.79],[157.79,157.94],[157.94,158.62],[158.62,158.99],[158.99,159.15],[159.15,159.52],[159.52,159.6],[159.6,159.97],[159.97,160.27],[160.27,160.5],[160.5,160.87]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Some supporters of repair favor place-based or class-based approaches for that reason.","start":161.76,"end":166.64,"words":[[161.8,162.01],[162.01,162.5],[162.5,162.64],[162.64,162.99],[162.99,163.35],[163.35,164.05],[164.05,164.12],[164.12,164.75],[164.75,165.39],[165.39,165.53],[165.53,165.74],[165.74,166.16]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Public opinion is divided: in a 2021 Pew survey, about 3 in 10 U.S. adults supported reparations, including about 77% of Black adults.","start":166.99,"end":178.44,"words":[[167.02,167.45],[167.45,167.94],[167.94,168.08],[168.08,168.71],[168.96,169.1],[169.1,169.24],[169.24,170.29],[170.29,170.5],[170.5,170.93],[171.17,171.52],[171.52,171.74],[171.74,171.88],[171.88,172.09],[172.09,172.44],[172.79,173.21],[173.21,173.7],[173.7,174.55],[174.79,175.36],[175.36,175.71],[175.71,176.97],[176.97,177.11],[177.11,177.4],[177.4,177.89]]},{"el":"h4","text":"What anyone can support","start":179.34,"end":180.99,"words":[[179.39,179.65],[179.65,180.17],[180.17,180.43],[180.43,180.86]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Even people who disagree about cash payments often support parts of repair: formal apologies, truth commissions, memorials, returning seized land (as with Bruce's Beach), clearing old laws and covenants, funding HBCUs, and investing in neighborhoods that were redlined or bulldozed.","start":181.69,"end":201.52,"words":[[181.74,182.06],[182.06,182.47],[182.47,182.63],[182.63,183.19],[183.19,183.6],[183.6,183.84],[183.84,184.48],[184.48,184.81],[184.81,185.21],[185.21,185.53],[185.53,185.69],[185.69,186.18],[186.46,186.86],[186.86,187.67],[187.95,188.28],[188.28,189.0],[189.28,190.17],[190.45,191.02],[191.02,191.34],[191.34,191.66],[191.66,191.83],[191.83,192.07],[192.07,192.55],[192.55,192.95],[193.24,193.8],[193.8,194.12],[194.12,194.37],[194.37,194.61],[194.61,195.42],[195.7,196.18],[196.18,197.07],[197.35,197.59],[197.59,198.24],[198.24,198.4],[198.4,199.13],[199.13,199.37],[199.37,199.53],[199.53,200.18],[200.18,200.26],[200.26,200.98]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Start where your community can agree.","start":201.87,"end":204.23,"words":[[201.92,202.2],[202.2,202.41],[202.41,202.55],[202.55,203.19],[203.19,203.4],[203.4,203.75]]}]}